  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Interface**\n\nI\'ve begun analyzing the interface based on the user\'s input and visual data. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the \"Brand & Shell\" elements. This includes the prominent \"ThingsAlive\" logo, featuring the atom/node cluster icon with blue and cyan elements, and the accompanying \"TELEMATICS IOT OS\" subtext. I\'m also examining the sidebar navigation, noting links to \"Dashboard\" and \"Alert\".\n\n\n**Defining the Features**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the features, now fleshing out the sidebar\'s functionalities. I\'m noting specific links like \"Alert Agent\", \"Admin,\" and the various subtabs under \"Admin\" (Industry Type, Sensor, etc.). I\'m also cataloging the \"Devices\" section with its management table and setup page, alongside \"Vendors,\" \"Users,\" \"Equipment\" (with add setup modal), \"Administrator,\" \"Diagnostics,\" and \"Settings.\" The sidebar\'s version information and header bar elements like the notification bell, theme toggle, and user profile are all noted.\n\n\n**Detailing the Sensors**\n\nNow, I\'m diving deeper into \"Admin -> Sensor\" management. I\'ve broken down the subtabs and noted the search filters for sensor names and industry type. The data table structure is clear, with details including the industry type, sensor name, and timestamps. I\'m also capturing the interactive elements like the view and edit actions, pagination, and the \"+ Add Sensor\" modal.\n\n**Mapping the Equipment**\n\nNext, I am documenting the \"Equipment Management\" screen. I\'ve noted the search criteria: details and status, and the \"+ Add Equipment\" button. Furthermore, I\'ve started logging the table structure, listing columns like ID and Equipment Name and the specific examples.\n\n\n**Cataloging the Equipment**\n\nI\'ve progressed to detailing the equipment data. I\'m noting elements like equipment descriptions, categories, maintenance plants, and CCL numbers. I\'ve broken down fields like manufacturers and model numbers, including specifics like the Volvo EC210 Crawler Excavator and their example CCL numbers. The \"+ Add Equipment\" modal is next in line, and I\'m capturing the form fields, like \"Equipment Name\", \"Category\", \"Maintenance Plant\" and \"CCL Number.\"\n\n\n\n**Describing the Tool Mapping**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Create Tool Mapping\" functionality. I\'ve noted the button and the table with columns for tool identifiers, industry types, mapped sensors, protocol, and update times. The \"Map Sensors to Tool Configuration\" modal is next on my list, including fields for tool names, target industry types, default telematics protocols, and a section for selecting and mapping sensors. I\'m focusing on the checkboxes and auto-calculation within the sensor mapping section.\n\n\n**Defining the \"Category\"**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Admin - Category\" section, identifying metric cards for total and inactive equipment. I\'ve broken down search functions and the \"+ Add Category\" button. My focus is on the category cards, each with code, creation date, equipment count, a status toggle, and edit/delete actions. I am also documenting the \"Add Equipment Category\" modal, and I am logging all form fields, from category name and code to the new powertrain specifications and description, and the save/cancel buttons.\n\n\n**Cataloging the Device Data**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Device Setup\" page within \"Device Management.\" I\'ve documented the table structure with its columns for ID, Device Name, IMEI Number, Equipment Name, Vendor, and Status, noting the displayed values. The action buttons, \"Edit\" and \"Delete,\" have also been logged. I\'m proceeding to document the \"Device Information & Tool Mapping\" form with simplified setup.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 861328994
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
