  planner_response {
    response: "I have built the **ThingsAlive Telematics IoT OS** web application to replicate the provided reference screens:\n\n- **Enterprise Brand & Shell**: Implemented the ThingsAlive telematics navigation with the signature atom/node emblem, dark/light theme toggle, language switcher, notification dropdown, and version indicator.\n- **Admin & Sensor Management** *(Screen 1)*: Created the master configuration console with searchable sensors, industry domain filtering, eye-action detail drawers, and pagination.\n- **Equipment Management & Setup** *(Screens 2 & 6)*: Formatted the 10-column equipment directory and the *Add New Equipment Setup* modal with engine specifications, CCL numbers, and plant assignments.\n- **Tool Mapping Engine** *(Screens 3 & 5)*: Built the *Map Sensors to Tool Configuration* profile manager with active telemetry channel checkboxes, real-time parameter tallying, and fieldbus protocol selectors.\n- **Equipment Categorization** *(Screens 7 & 8)*: Designed the metric summary cards (*Total Category*, *Total Equipment*, *Inactive Equipment*), interactive category cards with operational toggles, and the *Add Equipment Category* modal featuring dedicated *Powertrain & Fuel Specifications*.\n- **Device Management & Onboarding** *(Screens 9 & 11)*: Replicated the hardware telemetry registry with connectivity status indicators (*Online*/*Offline*), vendor filtering, and the dedicated *Device Information & Tool Mapping* onboarding workflow.\n- **Telematics AI & Documentation**: Added the floating documentation trigger and interactive *Ask AI* drawer capable of querying fleet diagnostics, sensor thresholds, and device states."
    thinking: "**Verifying Compilation Success**\n\nThe applet compiled without errors! Now, I\'m carefully reviewing the user request and the reference screens to make sure I completely understand the hotlinking aspect and how it impacts the website\'s design. I\'m focusing on the user\'s specification for the look and feel.\n\n\n**Defining UI Element Specs**\n\nI\'ve specified the visual elements for the application\'s UI, starting with the node/atom SVG logo and accompanying subtitle \"TELEMATICS IOT OS.\" I\'ve outlined the full sidebar navigation and footer with version information and a status indicator. The header is detailed with title, badge, notification, theme toggle, palette tool, language options, avatar, and sign-out button. Now I\'m focusing on the Admin - Sensor Management screen.\n\n\n**Detailing Admin Screen Specifications**\n\nNow I\'m diving into the specifics of the Admin screens. I\'ve broken down the \"Add Equipment\" button and the data table, including column names. For the \"Add New Equipment Setup\" modal, I\'m documenting all of the form fields and their data types. I\'m also specifying the \"Admin - Tool Mapping\" interface, from button and data fields to modal requirements, including how I will map sensors. Finally, I have specified how to manage tool mappings. I will now tackle the \"Admin - Category Management\" screen\'s metric cards, search functionality, and actions.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have built the **ThingsAlive Telematics IoT OS** web application to replicate the provided reference screens:\n\n- **Enterprise Brand & Shell**: Implemented the ThingsAlive telematics navigation with the signature atom/node emblem, dark/light theme toggle, language switcher, notification dropdown, and version indicator.\n- **Admin & Sensor Management** *(Screen 1)*: Created the master configuration console with searchable sensors, industry domain filtering, eye-action detail drawers, and pagination.\n- **Equipment Management & Setup** *(Screens 2 & 6)*: Formatted the 10-column equipment directory and the *Add New Equipment Setup* modal with engine specifications, CCL numbers, and plant assignments.\n- **Tool Mapping Engine** *(Screens 3 & 5)*: Built the *Map Sensors to Tool Configuration* profile manager with active telemetry channel checkboxes, real-time parameter tallying, and fieldbus protocol selectors.\n- **Equipment Categorization** *(Screens 7 & 8)*: Designed the metric summary cards (*Total Category*, *Total Equipment*, *Inactive Equipment*), interactive category cards with operational toggles, and the *Add Equipment Category* modal featuring dedicated *Powertrain & Fuel Specifications*.\n- **Device Management & Onboarding** *(Screens 9 & 11)*: Replicated the hardware telemetry registry with connectivity status indicators (*Online*/*Offline*), vendor filtering, and the dedicated *Device Information & Tool Mapping* onboarding workflow.\n- **Telematics AI & Documentation**: Added the floating documentation trigger and interactive *Ask AI* drawer capable of querying fleet diagnostics, sensor thresholds, and device states."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 139527436
    }
