 within these forms. Specifically, I\'m refactoring the `AddCategoryModal.tsx` file to dynamically populate its plant dropdown from the `plants: PlantItem[]` array, sourced from the Admin area. Also, for Tool Mappings, I am passing `availableSensors: SensorItem[]` from the Admin page. These data will define sensor selections when creating a tool mapping. This approach guarantees that only admin-defined values are used, eliminating any hardcoded options.\n\n\n**Enhancing Admin Data Flow**\n\nI\'ve achieved complete cohesiveness in the Admin system. Admin sensors feed tool mappings, and both the equipment and device forms draw directly from Admin data (sensors, categories, plants, mappings). New additions in Admin immediately appear as selectable options! I\'m now adding \"Add Plant\" functionality within the Admin\'s `PlantView`, allowing users to add plant details (name, location, code, active lines) which will then be accessible throughout the system.\n\n\n"
