  planner_response {
    response: "The **Device Form** and **Equipment Form** now strictly source and consume all configuration options\342\200\224**Sensors**, **Categories**, **Plants**, and **Tool Mappings**\342\200\224from the Admin master data catalog.\n\n### What Was Implemented\n\n- **Equipment Form Synchronization (`AddEquipmentModal`)**:\n  - **Categories & Plants**: Populated directly from Admin master data records, ensuring only active Admin facilities and equipment classifications can be chosen.\n  - **Tool Mapping Profile**: Directly binds to Admin Tool Mappings. Selecting a tool profile auto-populates its corresponding telemetry parameters and pre-checks its designated sensors.\n  - **Assigned Sensors**: Sourced dynamically from the master Admin sensor catalog (`SensorItem[]`), displaying real-time parameter chips and active sensor tags.\n\n- **Device Setup & Registration Form (`DeviceSetup`)**:\n  - **Plant & Category Selectors**: Replaced hardcoded option lists with reactive bindings to Admin `plants` and `categories`.\n  - **Tool Mapping Integration**: Linked directly to the Admin Tool Mapping suite. Selecting a profile immediately determines the protocol (e.g., *MODBUS TCP*, *CAN Bus (J1939)*) and activates the telemetry sensors mapped to that profile.\n  - **Interactive Sensor Mapping Matrix**: Shows the exact sensor channels and engineering parameters provisioned in the Admin master catalog.\n\n- **Unified Master Data Propagation (`AdminManagement` & `App.tsx`)**:\n  - **Bidirectional Consistency**: Any new Plant, Sensor, Category, or Tool Mapping added in the Admin module is instantly available in the dropdowns and multi-selects of both the Device and Equipment forms.\n  - **Admin Tool Mapping Builder**: Updated the sensor mapping modal to draw directly from registered Admin sensors, ensuring cross-module alignment.\n  - **Admin Plants Management**: Added plant creation with instant propagation to both forms and the fleet directory."
    thinking: "**Reviewing Device Mapping**\n\nI\'m now checking the plan\'s alignment with the initial intent, particularly the \"Admin page\" elements like sensors, categories, plants, and tool mappings. I\'m focusing on ensuring these values are correctly associated with \"device\" and \"equipment\" forms as specified. I\'m taking a close look at the mapping logic.\n\n\n**Refining UI Component Mapping**\n\nNow I\'m diving deeper into UI component mapping, examining the `AddEquipmentModal.tsx` and `DeviceSetup.tsx` files. I\'m focusing on the dynamic selects for categories, plants, and tool mappings, and how they interact and filter based on the Admin Master Data, ensuring proper data population and selection logic in the forms. I\'m also confirming that the sensor and telemetry displays behave as intended.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The **Device Form** and **Equipment Form** now strictly source and consume all configuration options\342\200\224**Sensors**, **Categories**, **Plants**, and **Tool Mappings**\342\200\224from the Admin master data catalog.\n\n### What Was Implemented\n\n- **Equipment Form Synchronization (`AddEquipmentModal`)**:\n  - **Categories & Plants**: Populated directly from Admin master data records, ensuring only active Admin facilities and equipment classifications can be chosen.\n  - **Tool Mapping Profile**: Directly binds to Admin Tool Mappings. Selecting a tool profile auto-populates its corresponding telemetry parameters and pre-checks its designated sensors.\n  - **Assigned Sensors**: Sourced dynamically from the master Admin sensor catalog (`SensorItem[]`), displaying real-time parameter chips and active sensor tags.\n\n- **Device Setup & Registration Form (`DeviceSetup`)**:\n  - **Plant & Category Selectors**: Replaced hardcoded option lists with reactive bindings to Admin `plants` and `categories`.\n  - **Tool Mapping Integration**: Linked directly to the Admin Tool Mapping suite. Selecting a profile immediately determines the protocol (e.g., *MODBUS TCP*, *CAN Bus (J1939)*) and activates the telemetry sensors mapped to that profile.\n  - **Interactive Sensor Mapping Matrix**: Shows the exact sensor channels and engineering parameters provisioned in the Admin master catalog.\n\n- **Unified Master Data Propagation (`AdminManagement` & `App.tsx`)**:\n  - **Bidirectional Consistency**: Any new Plant, Sensor, Category, or Tool Mapping added in the Admin module is instantly available in the dropdowns and multi-selects of both the Device and Equipment forms.\n  - **Admin Tool Mapping Builder**: Updated the sensor mapping modal to draw directly from registered Admin sensors, ensuring cross-module alignment.\n  - **Admin Plants Management**: Added plant creation with instant propagation to both forms and the fleet directory."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 951861811
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
