  planner_response {
    response: "I have updated the Equipment onboarding form to automatically pre-fill the **Engine Type** and **Fuel Tank Capacity** from the selected Admin Category:\n\n### What Was Implemented\n\n- **Automatic Specification Pre-filling**:\n  - In `AddEquipmentModal`, selecting any category from the **Category** dropdown immediately extracts the corresponding Admin category\'s `engineType` and `fuelTankCapacityLiters` and pre-populates both fields automatically.\n  - When the modal opens, the default category\'s specifications are loaded instantly, eliminating manual entry.\n\n- **Dropdown & Field Visual Feedback**:\n  - The Category dropdown options now display the category specifications inline (e.g., `Infrastructure Earthmovers (Diesel \342\200\242 400L Tank)`).\n  - Subtle indicator badges appear next to the **Engine Type** and **Fuel Tank (L)** labels to confirm they are pre-filled from the active Admin Category specifications, while remaining fully editable if adjustments are needed.\n\n- **End-to-End Master Data Binding**:\n  - Connected `EquipmentManagement` and `AddEquipmentModal` directly to the `CategoryItem[]` master data from the Admin catalog, ensuring changes or newly added categories in the Admin module immediately reflect their configured engine type and tank capacity in the Equipment form."
