  planner_response {
    response: "I will view lines 30 to 120 of `src/components/devices/DeviceSetup.tsx`."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Device Setup Fields**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `DeviceSetup.tsx` fields. Currently, I\'m focusing on Device Name, IMEI/Hardware Serial Number, Plant, Category, Equipment Assignment, and Hardware Vendor. I\'m moving on to a section regarding the Tool Mapping Profile, with strict source control.\n\n\n**Refining Tool Selection**\n\nI\'m now revising the tool selection process. My goal is to move beyond the pre-selected tool profile. I\'m introducing a \"Tool Name\" input field, mirroring the Admin Tool Mapping labels. This will include a datalist, populated from `toolMappings.map(t => t.toolName)`, for convenient selection, and the quick-select buttons.\n\n\n**Verifying Tool Matching Results**\n\nI\'ve just added logic to verify tool profile matches using a dynamic check, comparing the entered `toolName` against `toolMappings`. When a match is found, I\'m displaying a \"Tool Mapping Matched\" badge. I will provide protocol info, sensor counts, and parameter counts, extracted from the `matchedTool`. I\'m also preparing a dedicated box to break down the mapped sensors and parameters, showing their individual parameters! I will store the active sensors and parameters in state.\n\n\n**Detailing Mismatched State**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the behavior when no tool mapping is found. The grid now displays an empty state with a warning indicator: \"No Tool Mapping Match Found\". The state variables, `activeSensorNames` and `activeParametersMap`, are empty as expected, and the sensor grid\'s header reflects this with \"0 of [total] Connected \342\200\242 0 Parameters Active.\" I\'ve added a helpful message for manual selection. When a user clicks a sensor, it gets added to `activeSensorNames`.\n\n\n**Defining Submit Behavior**\n\nI\'m now examining form submission in `handleSubmit`. The `newDevice` object compiles data, including `toolProfile`, using a conditional. If `toolName` is empty, it defaults to the `matchedTool`\'s name or \"Manual Configuration\". I am also considering the default initialization of the `toolName` field and how that impacts the process: it is either an empty string or the matched tool name.\n\n\n**Implementing Dynamic Pre-population**\n\nI\'m now integrating dynamic pre-population based on user input for the tool name. If a user enters a valid tool name (e.g., \"Heavy Excavation Monitoring Kit (HE-400)\"), sensor and parameter data instantly loads. Conversely, clearing or editing the input triggers a display reset, enabling manual sensor selection. This direct response aligns perfectly with user intent. I am also implementing a datalist to facilitate easy admin tool selection.\n\n\n**Adding Tool Selection Options**\n\nI\'m now incorporating a datalist to enhance the \"Tool Name\" input. This datalist, dynamically populated with `toolMappings`, offers suggestions in the form of `{t.toolName} ({t.identifier})`. I\'ve included a clear button for resetting the field. Moreover, I\'ve integrated quick-select chips based on `toolMappings`, and will implement the logic to handle the tool selection button click.\n\n\n**Handling Tool Selection Buttons**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the logic for the quick-select buttons. When a user clicks a tool selection button, such as \"Heavy Excavation Monitoring Kit (HE-400)\", the corresponding tool name is entered into the \"Tool Name\" input. This action then triggers the matching logic I established previously. The display immediately updates based on this selection.\n\n\n**Addressing Manual Selection Conflicts**\n\nI\'m now refining the behavior when no tool mapping is found, specifically addressing conflict with previous manual selection. If `matchedTool` is null, a warning notice appears: \"No Tool Mapping match found for \'{toolName}\'. Sensors and parameters are empty \342\200\224 select sensors manually from the catalog below.\" I\'m ensuring that any existing manual selections in `activeSensorNames` are preserved, and that `activeSensorParams` remains intact. The display shows \"0 of 6 Connected \342\200\242 0 Parameters Active\" with the prompt: \"No sensors selected yet. Choose from the available Admin Sensors below.\"\n\n\n**Enabling Manual Parameter Control**\n\nI\'m now implementing the ability to toggle parameters for manually selected sensors. If a tool name matches, I display sensor and parameter data from that `toolMapping`. When there is no match, I display an empty state for manual selection. Now, each sensor card in the sensor grid will show its associated parameters, allowing users to toggle individual parameters on or off. This allows full control, whether using auto-filled or manual selection!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view lines 30 to 120 of `src/components/devices/DeviceSetup.tsx`."
    thinking_duration {
