cided to initialize `toolName` with `toolMappings[0]?.toolName || \'\'`. This should ensure that on the initial render, the sensors and parameters will show for the first tool in the list. This also means if I change `toolName` to anything non-matching, it\'ll immediately clear sensor and parameter info. I\'m also considering the user experience of initial empty state.\n\n\n**Revising Manual Input**\n\nI\'m now refining the manual input functionality for `DeviceSetup`. I\'m starting with an empty `toolName`, which gives an unmatched state with a clear \"Manual Mode\" indication. If the user then types a matching name, the component auto-populates, otherwise, the state remains empty for manual selection. I am considering options for the initial state for both new and returning users. The manual mode is now working great!\n\n\n**Enhancing Input and Matching**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on refining the interactive tool selection. Starting with an empty `toolName` field emphasizes manual entry. Quick-select buttons for all Admin Tool Mappings will be provided to aid selection. I\'m exploring direct population from suggested tool mappings, allowing users to match by click. The focus is on a robust and user-friendly matching workflow. The matching logic, as well as the updating, is now well-defined.\n\n\n**Synchronizing Data Updates**\n\nI\'m now implementing logic to ensure sensor and parameter updates happen correctly whenever `toolMappings` loads or `toolName` changes. I\'ve added a `useEffect` hook to handle the initial sync on mount. This ensures all state variables stay synchronized and the device setup remains robust. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and reliability.\n\n\n\n**Defining Data Display**\n\nI\'m now implementing the display logic for sensor and parameter info. I\'m prioritizing showing a card with key `matchedTool` data: identifier, protocol, sensor count, and active parameters. I\'m focusing on a clean, concise layout for the matched tool\'s profile for quick access. Further, I plan to display sensor and parameter details in an expandable view, accessible on click.\n\n\n**Refining Display Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the display of tool telemetry parameters. I\'ll include key details like sensor count and active parameters concisely. I\'m leveraging a visual component to ensure a clear indication that a tool mapping is loaded, and making it easy to see sensor/parameter counts. Further, I\'m working to make the data easy to find, as well as easy to update.\n\n\n**Implementing Parameter Highlighting**\n\nI\'m now implementing logic to highlight active parameters within the sensor catalog. The logic involves iterating through parameters of sensors and checking their presence in `activeParametersMap`. I\'m using dynamic classes for highlighting, which ensures an intuitive display. The visual emphasis will aid users in managing which parameters are currently active. I also updated the styling based on the existing components.\n\n\n**Defining Empty State**\n\nI\'m now focused on handling the \'no match\' scenario when the `toolName` is empty or custom. I\'m implementing an informative notice box to display when the tool isn\'t matched. I\'m also now showing a message in the Sensors and Parameters Catalog. I\'m focusing on providing users clear feedback. I also plan to show the activity indicator for sensor catalog.\n\n\n**Implementing Sensor Activation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on activating sensors and their parameters through user interaction. Clicking a sensor adds it to `activeSensorNames`. Then, clicking parameter tags toggles their active status, modifying `activeParameters`. I\'ve also implemented handling the \"no sensors\" message display. The user can now click sensor cards and activate their parameters.\n\n\n**Improving Tool Selection**\n\nI\'ve just refined the interactive tool selection buttons, making it easy to see all options. Tool names can be directly populated from the list. The current matching workflow is now working well, and is easy to use. I\'m focusing on simplicity.\n\nI\'ve also introduced an easy option to clear the currently selected tool, for a fresh start with \"manual mode\" entry.\n\n\n"
