  planner_response {
    response: "I have implemented the Tool Name matching logic in the Device Creation flow:\n\n- **Admin Tool Name Matching**:\n  - In the device creation form, users can type or select a **Tool Name**.\n  - **Matched State**: When the entered Tool Name matches an existing tool mapping from the Admin catalog (e.g., *Heavy Excavation Monitoring Kit (HE-400)* or *Crusher Vibration Telematics Kit*), the system displays a positive match badge, auto-populates the associated sensors, and loads their corresponding parameter channels.\n  - **Unmatched / Empty State**: When the Tool Name does not match or is left empty, the sensors and parameters are kept empty by default, allowing the user to manually select sensors and parameter channels directly from the sensor catalog.\n  - **Quick-Select Chips**: Included quick chips for all Admin tool mappings for fast testing and pre-filling, along with a \"Clear / Manual Mode\" button."
    thinking: "**Verifying Equipment Fields**\n\nThe system build is complete! Now, I\'m focusing on validating the equipment form fields. Specifically, I\'m checking that selecting an admin category automatically populates engine type and tank capacity fields, ensuring proper data flow and streamlined user experience. I want to make certain that no requirements were missed during development.\n\n\n"
