  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Apply consistent theme colors** (IMPLEMENTATION): The user requested: \"Can you use the same theme colours\". This is in response to the recent implementation of the `DeviceSetup.tsx` flow. The goal is to ensure all UI elements (buttons, borders, backgrounds, text) in the newly created components align with the established design system observed in the existing application (e.g., `#FF4D00` for accents, `#FDFCF5` for light mode backgrounds).\n\n2. User Knowledge\n- **Preferences/Requests:** The user explicitly requested: \"Can you use the same theme colours\".\n- **Context:** The user provided a screenshot (`Screenshot 2026-09-07 at 1.07.55\342\200\257PM.png`) showing the application\'s current UI, which has been used to verify the color palette against the codebase.\n\n3. Work Accomplished\n- **Tool Name Matching Logic:** Implemented the matching logic in `src/components/devices/DeviceSetup.tsx`. When a user enters a Tool Name, the system automatically populates sensors and parameters if a match is found in the Admin Tool Mappings.\n- **TypeScript Fixes:** Resolved `TS2339` errors related to `activeParametersMap` by correctly handling array types and existence checks during the `useMemo` calculation of `totalActiveParameters`.\n- **Component Discovery:** Mapped the global color palette and component architecture by inspecting `src/index.css`, `src/components/Sidebar.tsx`, `src/components/Header.tsx`, and `src/components/admin/SensorTable.tsx`.\n- **Build Verification:** Confirmed that the application compiles successfully after all changes.\n\n4. Model Knowledge\n- **Design System/Palette:**\n  - **Accent:** `#FF4D00` (Used for primary actions, active states, and highlights).\n  - **Background (Light):** `#FDFCF5` (Global body background).\n  - **Background (Dark):** `#121212` / `#151514`.\n  - **Borders:** `#121212/15` (light mode), `white/15` (dark mode).\n  - **Text:** `#121212` (light mode), `#FDFCF5` (dark mode).\n- **Architecture:** The application uses a central state management approach in `src/App.tsx`, where core data (`sensors`, `toolMappings`, `categories`, `equipmentList`, `devices`, `plants`) is passed down to sub-components. `DeviceSetup.tsx` is a sub-route of the `devices` tab.\n- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS is used. Global styles are defined in `src/index.css`, which includes custom classes like `.bg-accent`, `.text-accent`, and `.border-accent`.\n\n5. Files and Code\n- **Edited Files:**\n  - `/src/components/devices/DeviceSetup.tsx`: Implemented tool name matching, sensor/parameter state management, and manual override capabilities.\n- **Viewed Files:**\n  - `/src/index.css`: Defines the global design system (colors, fonts, scrollbars).\n  - `/src/components/Sidebar.tsx`: Reference for sidebar layout and navigation styling.\n  - `/src/components/Header.tsx`: Reference for header layout and theme toggling logic.\n  - `/src/components/admin/AdminManagement.tsx`: Reference for admin tab structure.\n  - `/src/components/admin/SensorTable.tsx`: Reference for table layout and filter styling.\n  - `/src/App.tsx`: Reference for main application state and routing.\n\n6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Immediate Next Step:** Review the implementation in `src/components/devices/DeviceSetup.tsx` and apply the consistent theme colors identified in `src/index.css`.\n- **Action Plan:**\n  1. Audit `src/components/devices/DeviceSetup.tsx` for any hardcoded colors or inconsistent styling.\n  2. Replace any non-standard colors with the established Tailwind utility classes or custom CSS classes (e.g., using `bg-accent` or the specific hex codes found in `index.css`).\n  3. Ensure that the \"Matched\" and \"Unmatched\" states in the `DeviceSetup` component visually align with the rest of the application\'s UI components (like the `SensorTable` or `AdminManagement` views)."
    included_step_index_start: 125
    included_step_index_end: 180
    conversation_log_uris: "file:///.aistudio/artifacts/brain/f57dea6d-3083-4e4d-91af-4cd0e2dcc8d6/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl"
