    session_summary: "### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Pre-fill engine type and tank capacity in equipment form based on category** (NOT STARTED):\n  - **User Intent:** \"See in the admin category, we are filling engine type and tank capacity, so when i am selecting a category in the equipment form, it should pre-fill the values of tank capacity and engine type.\"\n  - **Status:** NOT STARTED. This is the primary remaining task.\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n- **Preferences/Requests:**\n  - \"See in the admin category, we are filling engine type and tank capacity, so when i am selecting a category in the equipment form, it should pre-fill the values of tank capacity and engine type.\"\n  - \"in admin tool mapping we are giving the tool name, in device creation if tool name is matching with tool mapping data it should show the sensors and parameters info, other wise show empty user will select manually\"\n  - \"Can you use the same theme colours\"\n- **Context:**\n  - The user provided a screenshot (`Screenshot 2026-09-07 at 1.07.55\342\200\257PM.png`) to define the desired UI theme, which was used to update the global design system and component styling.\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n- **Tool Name Matching Logic (IMPLEMENTATION):** Implemented in `src/components/devices/DeviceSetup.tsx`. The system now automatically populates sensors and parameters if a match is found in the Admin Tool Mappings; otherwise, it defaults to manual selection.\n- **UI Theme Implementation (IMPLEMENTATION):** Updated the application\'s global design system to match the provided screenshot:\n  - **Global Styles:** Updated `src/index.css` with new color palette (`#0B7285` for accents, `#F4F7FB` for light backgrounds, `#1E293B` for text).\n  - **Sidebar:** Updated `src/components/Sidebar.tsx` to align with the new theme, including logo and navigation styling.\n  - **Header:** Updated `src/components/Header.tsx` to match the new layout, icons, and theme toggle functionality.\n  - **Admin Management:** Updated `src/components/admin/AdminManagement.tsx` to use pill-style tab buttons with icons.\n  - **Sensor Table:** Updated `src/components/admin/SensorTable.tsx` to match the new table styling, headers, and action buttons.\n- **TypeScript Fixes:** Resolved `TS2339` errors related to `activeParametersMap` by correctly handling array types and existence checks.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Design System/Palette:**\n  - **Accent:** `#0B7285` (Primary actions, active states).\n  - **Background (Light):** `#F4F7FB`.\n  - **Text (Light):** `#1E293B`.\n  - **Borders:** `#E2E8F0` (light), `#334155` (dark).\n- **Architecture:**\n  - The application uses a central state management approach in `src/App.tsx`, passing core data (`sensors`, `toolMappings`, `categories`, `equipmentList`, `devices`, `plants`) to sub-components.\n  - `DeviceSetup.tsx` handles the device onboarding flow.\n  - `AdminManagement.tsx` manages sub-tabs for administrative entities.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n- **Edited Files:**\n  - `/src/components/devices/DeviceSetup.tsx`: Implemented tool name matching logic and manual override capabilities.\n  - `/src/index.css`: Updated global design system variables and scrollbar styling.\n  - `/src/components/Sidebar.tsx`: Updated navigation layout and styling to match the new theme.\n  - `/src/components/Header.tsx`: Updated header layout, icons, and theme toggle logic.\n  - `/src/components/admin/AdminManagement.tsx`: Updated sub-tab navigation to use pill-style buttons with icons.\n  - `/src/components/admin/SensorTable.tsx`: Updated table layout, headers, and action buttons to match the new design.\n- **Viewed Files:**\n  - `/src/components/AskAIWidget.tsx`: Inspected for consistency with the overall UI theme.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Immediate Next Step:** Implement the category-based pre-filling logic in the equipment form.\n- **Action Plan:**\n  1. Locate the equipment form component (likely within `src/components/devices/` or `src/components/equipment/`).\n  2. Identify the state management for \"Category\" selection.\n  3. Implement a listener or `useEffect` that triggers when the category changes, fetching the corresponding \"engine type\" and \"tank capacity\" from the `categories` data and updating the form fields accordingly.\n- **Relevant Files:**\n  - `src/components/equipment/EquipmentForm.tsx` (or equivalent, need to locate the specific file for the equipment form)."
