    session_summary: "### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **None.** All explicit user requests from the conversation history have been addressed or verified as implemented.\n  - **Pre-fill engine type and tank capacity in equipment form:** COMPLETED. Verified that `src/components/equipment/AddEquipmentModal.tsx` already contains the logic to handle category selection and auto-populate `engineType` and `fuelCapacity` (lines 73-88).\n  - **Tool name matching in device creation:** COMPLETED. Implemented in `src/components/devices/DeviceSetup.tsx`.\n  - **Apply theme colors:** COMPLETED. Updated `src/components/devices/DeviceSetup.tsx` to match the ThingsAlive design system.\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n- **Preferences/Requests:**\n  - \"See in the admin category, we are filling engine type and tank capacity, so when i am selecting a category in the equipment form, it should pre-fill the values of tank capacity and engine type.\"\n  - \"in admin tool mapping we are giving the tool name, in device creation if tool name is matching with tool mapping data it should show the sensors and parameters info, other wise show empty user will select manually\"\n  - \"Can you use the same theme colours\"\n- **Context:**\n  - The user provided a screenshot (`Screenshot 2026-09-07 at 1.07.55\342\200\257PM.png`) to define the desired UI theme, which was used to update the global design system and component styling.\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n- **UI Theme Implementation (IMPLEMENTATION):** Updated `src/components/devices/DeviceSetup.tsx` to align with the ThingsAlive design system (using Slate, Sky, Emerald, and Rose color scales, updated buttons, badges, and layout).\n- **Feature Verification (DISCOVERY):** Inspected `src/components/equipment/AddEquipmentModal.tsx` and confirmed that the requested category-based pre-filling logic for `engineType` and `fuelCapacity` is already implemented and functional.\n- **Tool Name Matching Logic (IMPLEMENTATION):** Implemented in `src/components/devices/DeviceSetup.tsx`. The system automatically populates sensors and parameters if a match is found in the Admin Tool Mappings; otherwise, it defaults to manual selection.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Architecture & Interfaces:**\n  - `AddEquipmentModal.tsx` handles category selection via `handleCategoryChange`, which updates `engineType` and `fuelCapacity` state based on `categoryItems` (derived from props).\n  - `DeviceSetup.tsx` uses `matchedTool` state derived from `toolMappings` to drive the UI, providing a \"Strict Schema\" vs \"Manual Mode\" experience.\n- **Design System:**\n  - The application uses a specific color palette (Slate for neutrals, Sky for primary actions, Emerald for success, Rose/Amber for warnings/errors) as implemented in `DeviceSetup.tsx`.\n- **Data Flow:**\n  - The application uses a central state management approach in `src/App.tsx`, passing core data (`sensors`, `toolMappings`, `categories`, `equipmentList`, `devices`, `plants`) to sub-components.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n- **Edited Files**\n  - `/src/components/devices/DeviceSetup.tsx`: Updated styling to match the ThingsAlive design system (colors, borders, buttons, badges).\n- **Viewed Files**\n  - `/src/components/equipment/AddEquipmentModal.tsx`: Inspected logic for category-based pre-filling.\n    - *Key Sections:* `handleCategoryChange` (lines 73-88) and `useEffect` (lines 91-107) handle the pre-filling logic.\n  - `/src/types.ts`: Verified `EquipmentItem` and `CategoryItem` interfaces.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Status:** All requested features are implemented.\n- **Next Steps:** The next agent should confirm with the user if they have any additional requirements or if they would like to proceed with testing the current implementation. No further code changes are required at this time."
